{
  "note": [
    "The Escape Pod's fabric (DR-109), cut from the one Feinstein layout in scripts/fabric-feinstein.mjs, in Deck Nine's frame -- regenerate from there, do not hand-edit. ESCAPE-POD v1 to RoomPolishInstructions/ESCAPE-POD_Visual-Design-Handoff_v1/ESCAPE-POD/DR-109-GEOMETRY-DEV-ANSWER.md (approved by the user, 14 Sep): the floor plan of Deck Nine's accepted TURN-270 POD-DOOR-OPEN glimpse, pod = Deck Nine + [5.6, 0, 0].",
    "A 4.0 m cabin, level with Deck Nine's deck, under a ribbed barrel vault (the `vault` part: chord 2.4 at the floor, crown 2.4, widest 3.0 at 0.9 m). THE ROOM AS YOU MEET IT FROM DECK NINE, which is how the user described it (DR-112): WEBBING ON THE LEFT ONLY, THE CONTROL PANEL ON THE BACK BULKHEAD, A LARGE PORTHOLE ON THE RIGHT ONLY. Left is south, right is north, back is west. The webbing is one mass filling the south side, its near strap plane at z -0.55 and its back curtain on the hull at 1.40 -- one mass, which is also the plainer reading of canon, \"a mass of safety webbing ... fills half the pod\". The open floor is the north strip, and THIS ROOM'S EYE STANDS IN IT at z -0.85, not at the middle of the box: the middle is inside the webbing. The eye inside the webbing is a room of its own, ESCAPE-POD-WEB.",
    "THE PORTHOLE IS ON THE NORTH FLANK, opposite the webbing, and ENLARGED by DR-112 to 2.4 x 1.1 from 1.9 x 0.9 -- sixty per cent more pane -- centred 1.25 m up so a seated eye looks straight through its middle. It is a WELL, not a hole: the hull here is the vault's curved flank, so a flat pane cannot lie in it; the recess is 0.18 m deep, which is how a window in a pressure hull is built anyway and gives the painter a rim with depth. THE CONSOLE MOVED OFF THIS FLANK to the back (west) bulkhead to free it, and the service column moved to the back-south corner to make room for the console. Nothing else stands on the north side.",
    "East, the one door: the pod's east wall is Deck Nine's west wall, the same 1.6 x 2.0 m opening, and the leaf is Deck Nine's own part (POD-DOOR without OPENBIT), 0.35 m beyond the pod's wall face behind the pod-side frame. Open, while the pod is docked (BLOWUP-COUNTER < 5): Deck Nine's channel straight to the shut starboard bulkhead 9.05 m off, the gangway mouth on the left with its bulkhead down, the sanitation alcove on the right. Both emergency bulkheads are drawn shut here whatever the game says, because the pod door is only ever open to Deck Nine after they have crashed shut. After launch nothing of Deck Nine is drawn."
  ],
